cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use geotruth, its corpus or its expected answers in your work, please cite it as
  below, and state the versions you used: the geotruth commit or release, the corpus
  version and the engine version (they are recorded in corpus/MANIFEST.json,
  corpus/expected/MANIFEST.json and every result file).
title: "geotruth: exact ground truth for computational geometry"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Abdulfayyod
    family-names: Mukhamedov
repository-code: "https://github.com/abafaboy/geotruth"
url: "https://github.com/abafaboy/geotruth"
abstract: >-
  geotruth is an exact-answer conformance suite for computational-geometry libraries.
  Every IEEE-754 double is a rational number, so the DE-9IM relation, the overlay and the
  validity of two geometries have exactly one correct answer, which geotruth computes in
  exact integer and rational arithmetic on the input doubles, with two independent routes
  for relate and an independent certificate for overlay. A corpus of near-degenerate cases
  is run through adapters for GEOS, JTS, Boost.Geometry, Clipper2, CGAL, georust geo and
  several JavaScript libraries, and each answer is graded against the exact one within the
  library's own documented precision model. The code is MIT-licensed; the corpus and the
  expected answers are dedicated to the public domain (CC0 1.0).
keywords:
  - computational geometry
  - exact arithmetic
  - robustness
  - conformance testing
  - DE-9IM
  - polygon overlay
  - OGC Simple Features
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-26"
